/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 48 0 R
/T (North Korean state-sponsored threat actors have weaponized social engineering, particularly phishing attacks, to create a growing "fake employee" problem. These operatives secure legitimate positions at companies worldwide, funneling their salaries back to the DPRK regime. Recent campaigns demonstrate an urgent need for reliable identity verification before the hiring process begins. This report examines how falsified identities backed by stolen or fabricated credentials are penetrating organizations, and explores verification tools that can prevent these single points of failure.)
/E (North Korean state-sponsored threat actors have weaponized social engineering, particularly phishing attacks, to create a growing "fake employee" problem. These operatives secure legitimate positions at companies worldwide, funneling their salaries back to the DPRK regime. Recent campaigns demonstrate an urgent need for reliable identity verification before the hiring process begins. This report examines how falsified identities backed by stolen or fabricated credentials are penetrating organizations, and explores verification tools that can prevent these single points of failure.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [5]
>>
